    <event>
      <start>-176</start>
      <end>-176</end>
      <text>The First Convening</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>History</category>
      <description>The first convening is held, a gathering of 17 Gods each of whom had witnessed the first death, organized by the God of Fulgurite, to discuss what they had seen.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
    <event>
      <start>-176</start>
      <end>-176</end>
      <text>Afterlife Star</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>Star</category>
      <description>Created by the God of Chromodynamic Energy following the First Convening. They would conclude that there must be an afterlife and would, with Fulgurite, found the first religion.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
    <event>
      <start>-147</start>
      <end>-147</end>
      <text>Great Oceanic Crater Created</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>Geography</category>
      <description>A territory dispute between Carbon and Calcium—both defending their lesser-Gods—leads to a fight and the creation of the Great Oceanic Crater.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
    <event>
      <start>-147</start>
      <end>-147</end>
      <text>First Crater System</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>Star</category>
      <description>Minor star system created shortly after the fight between Calcium and Carbon. The star documents the creation of the Great Oceanic Crater.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
    <event>
      <start>-145</start>
      <end>-145</end>
      <text>First God Council Held</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>History</category>
      <description>Having seen the aftermath of the fight between Calcium and Carbon, Life and Death call for the first truce of the war, though only temporary. No consensus is reached and the war continues to rage on.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
    <event>
      <start>-140</start>
      <end>-140</end>
      <text>Mitosis System</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>Star</category>
      <description>The first three stars of this system were published by Hydrogen Cyanide, including descriptions on how to create the organisms which they had invented. The system would explode into chaos as other Gods built upon the idea, each publishing their own findings.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
    <event>
      <start>-116</start>
      <end>-116</end>
      <text>Carbonprint System</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>Star</category>
      <description>Despite the inventor of animals having released no star detailing their creation, it would not go unnoticed. It is likely neighboring Gods detected something attacking their territory, and the discovery of animals would lead them to publish these stars, which would garner attention and quickly become systems.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
    <event>
      <start>-140</start>
      <end>-140</end>
      <text>Organisms Invented</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>Biology</category>
      <description>Inspired by material discussed during the first council, the God of Hydrogen Cyanide invents the first organisms as a means of autonomous warfare, putting Gods in less danger. These organisms would be incredibly complex, but also simultaneously very basal compared to the forms they would soon begin to spread out and adapt into.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
    <event>
      <start>-130</start>
      <end>-130</end>
      <text>Multicellular Life Invented</text>
      <progress>0</progress>
      <fuzzy>False</fuzzy>
      <fuzzy_start>False</fuzzy_start>
      <fuzzy_end>False</fuzzy_end>
      <locked>False</locked>
      <ends_today>False</ends_today>
      <category>Biology</category>
      <description>The first multicellular life is invented, though this invention would be seen many more times seperately, the first time is documented in the Zygote system.</description>
      <default_color>192,192,192</default_color>
    </event>
